<title>JAPAN: Japan average rates on time deposits.</title>
<headline>Japan average rates on time deposits.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of more than 10 million yen in the week to December 4 as released by the Bank of Japan on Wednesday:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.34 (0.34)	 one year     0.37 (0.37)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.34 (0.34)	 two years    0.45 (0.46)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.35 (0.35)	 three years  0.91 (0.94)</p>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of three to 10 million yen:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.30 (0.30)	 one year     0.32 (0.32)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.30 (0.30)	 two years    0.40 (0.40)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.30 (0.30)	 three years  0.86 (0.89)</p>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of less than three million yen:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.25 (0.25)	 one year     0.28 (0.28)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.25 (0.25)	 two years    0.35 (0.36)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.25 (0.25)	 three years  0.81 (0.84)</p>
<p>Average rates on certificates of deposit, Dec 02 - Dec 06:</p>
<p>    less than 30 days  0.49 (0.49)   120-150 days  0.54 (0.52)</p>
<p>    30-60 days	   0.50 (0.51)   150-180 days  0.60 (UNQ )</p>
<p>    60-90 days	   0.51 (0.51)   180-360 days  0.49 (0.53)</p>
<p>    90-120 days	  0.51 (0.51)   over 360 days 0.58 (0.75)</p>
</text>
